      "message": "fix(post): Mazak post writes S.. M3/M4 and M5, not MOTON/MOTOFF\n\nThe Mazak post started the spindle with `MOTON S..` and stopped it with\n`MOTOFF`: multi-letter words outside RS-274 / ISO 6983 that state no\ndirection ahead of a G84 right-hand rigid tap. It now writes `S<rpm> M3`\n(`S<rpm> M4` for a left-hand-cut mill, PARAM MillSpindle reverse, #988 -\nthe post declares millSpindleReverse like fanuc.cps) and `M5`, in the\nsame places in the program. The Mazak goldens change only on those lines.\n\nPinned by crates/post/tests/mazak_spindle_words.rs. Decision in\ndocs/decisions/1411-mazak-iso-spindle.md.\n\nFixes #1411\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
